<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haqqi al-Azm</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1864–1955</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haqqi al-Azm was a Syrian politician from the prominent Azm family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> and a supporter of cooperation with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. He was appointed first governor of the State of Damascus under the French Mandate in 1920, and he later served as Prime Minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> from 1932 to 1934, heading a government with limited powers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haqqi-al-azm.jpg" alt="Haqqi al-Azm" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haqqi_al-Azm.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
